% A csv table read as RFC 4180 writes it: a header skipped, lines ending in
% a carriage return and a line feed, quoted fields holding commas, doubled
% quotes and a line end of their own, and an empty field quoted or not.  A
% quoted field is typed after its quotes are removed, so "eve" is a symbol
% and "7" an integer.  The same table imported again with its middle
% column skipped adds facts of another arity, and the two rows for dee are
% one fact.
person(N, C, A)?
age(N, A)?
